"DESIGN task: derive the ~6 available battle actions from stance x armament LOADOUTS instead of the stat-block union. Synthesis of the four candidate designs (2026-08-12): designs C+D compose into the core model -- (1) TECHNIQUE: an acquirable asset granting a battle action, carrying armament requirements as data (requires spear, requires free hand, none); (2) STANCE: ~6 technique slots + stat contributions + armament-kind requirements; FORCED stances (prone, disarmed/improvised) have no armament requirements and are entered by effects, not choice; (3) LOADOUT: a prepared pairing of stance + armament set, validated AT PREPARATION TIME in the menu (fail fast at assignment, never at runtime): a technique may only be slotted where the loadout's armaments satisfy its requirements, and forced stances only admit requirement-free techniques; (4) swap-loadout is itself a one-round battle action; (5) the active loadout FULLY determines the battle-action set (utility actions like move stay outside the six, from baseline/traits as today). Rejected as cores but kept as sub-tools: value-ranking (design A) never gates availability -- possibly useful for AI action choice or suggested default assignments; conditional offers (design B) survive only as technique requirement METADATA consumed by preparation-time validation, never evaluated mid-fight. Open problems recorded in comments."